			<div class="content" id="post-content-4838255">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Comedy / Bizarre (if that counts as a category)</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>According to the public, the elevator was invented and popularized in the late 1800's.</li>
<li>In actuality, the first elevators popped up around 3000 BC.</li>
<li>Functional elevators can be found in historic buildings; there's even ancient Egyptian elevators in the great pyramids.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
The containment procedures and description serve to introduce the anomaly and explain how the Foundation is handling it. The Foundation puts out the story that the first elevator was installed in 1880, and whenever they find an elevator created before that date, they either destroy it, conceal it, or make it look like a modern elevator. It also serves to justify some aspects of the anomaly, like how elevators could be invented before electricity, or how knowledge of how to build an elevator could propagate in the first place.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Then there's an addendum explaining some notable examples of ancient elevators, which serve both to clarify the anomaly further and act as their own interesting anecdotes. Examples I have in mind are solid stone elevators installed into the great pyramids, how elevators are used in various medieval castles, and possibly even mentions of elevators in the bible.</p>
<p>The resolution to the SCP comes in the form of an MTF log. Foundation satellites detect an object manifest in space and slowly descend to the earth's surface. An MTF squad is deployed to the estimated landing zone, and discover it to be a descending elevator. When it hits the surface, aliens pop out, and explain that 4000 yeas ago, they gave the gift of elevators to man, having misinterpreted instructions from the alien queen to &quot;uplift&quot; our species.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
It might be ambitious for a first SCP, but if I go with the &quot;aliens taught us how to make elevators&quot; story, the hook could be that the object class is Explained, with the subclass of Keter, since even though the anomaly is explained the phenomenon still requires coverup procedures.</p>
<p>Alternatively, the hook could just be an incredibly jarring phrase in the containment procedures, like &quot;Highly visible elevators installed in notable historic sites, such as the main lobby elevator of the Great Pyramid of Giza&#8230;&quot;.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
Some of my favorite SCPs are the ones that are just about something straight up bizarre, like 5940 or 5319 or 2598 or 4062. Something about them appeals to me in a huge way, more than horror or drama ever does in SCPs. It's definitely what I wanna try for my first SCP, if it wouldn't be too much of a challenge.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
