<p>Ahh, thank you for the review, you raise some good points.</p>
<p>What if, instead of the art of elevator installation propagating throughout human culture on it's own, it's isolated incidents of ancient people being told how to make an elevator? The foundation's treatment of the anomaly would probably then be more justified. I guess that would also partially justify the aliens only visiting after 4000 years (which should actually have said 5000 cuz I'm bad at math).</p>
<p>As for your last concern, what if I focused the reveal less on &quot;how are ancient people building elevators?&quot;, and more on &quot;why are ancient people being taught how to build elevators?&quot;? I could say/imply right out of the gate that it's goofy green aliens, and I could keep the punchline where they've misconstrued the meaning of &quot;uplift&quot;.</p>

							</div>

								
					
