			<div class="content" id="post-content-4851355">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Behold!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I absolutely love this. As I was reading I was concerned that this lacked a punchline, but you cleared that quickly.</p>
<p>A few points of advice.<br />
Make sure that list of elevators does not drag and has a rise in bizarreness. You shouldn't start with the pyramids or a recognizable location. You should also expound upon how these machines work, mainly for world building and such. There's some cool imagery here that could be fun reading.</p>
<p>I'm not sure an MTF log is exactly needed. That could be taking up unnecessary space to establish team members, what they're doing, and so on before all the action. Keep the whole satellite detection point, but just have a Foundation doctor communicate over a transmission system of some sort. You should be going for the energy of <a href="/scp-3197">SCP-3197</a>.</p>
<p>I do feel like the aliens landing on Earth is unneeded. If their whole MO was to &quot;uplift&quot; the human species, them coming back every, say, 1000 years to monitor the Earth would make a bit more sense and also explain why the Foundation has never interacted with them before.</p>
<p>Definite <span style="color: green"><strong>greenlight</strong></span> from me. Good luck and be sure to reach out to other reviewers!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

